WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
Hey everyone, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily Episode 522.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:12.260
I'm Patrick in Vancouver, today is June 25th, 2026. Plenty going on in EV land, let's get to it.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.720
Tesla's dry electrode pattern adds a protective coating to PTFE binder particles,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.640
to stop lithium ions from breaking them down inside the cell.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.480
The filing explains that PTFE particles receive an ionically insulating yet

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.480
electrically conductive shell before fibrillization.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Materials such as carbon black, graphene or copper form that shell through mechanical fusion.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.180
The coating blocks lithium ions and electrons from stripping fluorine out of the polymer

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.700
and forming lithium fluoride. Coverage targets at least 70% of the particle surface,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:54.520
with 90% listed as preferred. The entire sequence remains solvent-free and works with existing

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:00.240
high-speed roll-to-roll electrode lines. From cell level chemistry, the next question is how

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:06.620
that stored energy actually gets used once it leaves the pack. Tesla, Sun Run and Renew home

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:12.200
announced a partnership to aggregate powerwall and partner batteries into a 16 gigawatt virtual

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.960
power plant. The project combines residential systems across the United States to provide grid

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:23.820
services at scale. The company's described the effort as the largest distributed energy resource

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:29.800
in the country. For Tesla, the move adds meaningful volume to the energy division while automotive

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:36.000
margins remain under pressure. Deployment will draw on both existing home batteries and new customer

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.880
signups. The partnership gives the energy business a clearer growth path separate from vehicle

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:48.160
production cycles. Reports note that energy revenue could outweigh deliveries in the Q2 narrative

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:54.120
because storage deployments have shown steady increases while automotive margins face pressure.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:02:01.480
The 16 gigawatt virtual power plant adds visible scale to the division. Investors are watching whether

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:07.100
deployments accelerate further in the second half of the year. The segment offers a different growth

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:13.380
profile from vehicle production cycles. Energy storage growth is therefore positioned as a potential

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:19.840
larger story than vehicle numbers this quarter. Grid scale aggregation raises practical questions about

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:26.760
how individual vehicles are stored and charged at retail sites. Four Tesla vehicles caught fire at a

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:32.680
dealership in Owings Mills, Maryland. Local fire crews responded to the incident and the cause remains

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:39.320
under investigation. Dealership fires involving multiple vehicles stay uncommon yet draw attention to

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:45.460
storage and charging practices on site. Tesla has not released details on what protocols were in place

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:52.040
or any changes under consideration. The event adds one more operational consideration for the retail

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:58.960
network even when such incidents remain rare. Retail site questions stand in contrast to third-party

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:06.340
hardware that aims to improve the charging experience itself. Xiaomi introduced a robotic arm that

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:11.400
locates a parked electric vehicle and connects the charging plug without driver input.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:17.280
The system revives an early Tesla automated charging concept that was never brought to market.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:23.740
Xiaomi's version targets residential driveways and fleet parking lots. The launch shows continued

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:30.300
industry interest in removing manual steps from daily charging routines. Tesla has not announced

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:36.980
comparable hardware since the original idea first appeared. Tesla China added integration with the

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:45.740
Dubai AI model for in-car features. China's public EV charger network exceeded 22.49 million units.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.840
Other automakers announced further expansion of local production outside China.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:57.260
The charger milestone reflects continued infrastructure build out in the world's largest EV market.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:04.020
Tesla's AI integration follows similar moves by domestic brands to enhance voice and assistance

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:10.040
systems. While one company works on automating the plug, another is trying to lower the price of

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:16.720
the vehicle that needs charging. Slate auto backed by Jeff Bezos and led by former Tesla and Amazon

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:24.980
executives announced plans for an electric pickup starting at $24,950. Ross Gerber noted the pricing

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:30.540
and suggested Amazon could become a fleet buyer. The vehicle positions itself as a lower cost

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:36.620
option in the small truck segment compared with current electric pickups. Production and availability

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:42.840
timelines have not yet been detailed. New vehicle competition pairs with fresh activity in the

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:50.140
Robotaxi space. Amazon's Zooks revealed an updated purpose-built Robotaxi without traditional controls.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.960
The revised design supports wider commercial deployment plans for the Amazon subsidiary.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:02.420
The move adds another dedicated player to the Robotaxi segment alongside Tesla's CyberCab program.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.540
Regulatory developments will shape how quickly any of these vehicles can operate at scale.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.700
The United Nations Economic Commission for Europe adopted a new global framework for automated

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:19.380
driving systems. The rules set baseline requirements that Tesla's unsupervised

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:26.480
FSD and CyberCab programs would need to meet for international markets. The decision creates a

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:33.900
clearer certification path in Europe and regions that follow UNECE standards. Manufacturers are now

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:41.680
assessing how the guidelines affect timelines already in development. Yesterday's FSD V14.3.3

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:48.440
rollout in Australia shows software still moving forward even as regulators work on these broader frameworks.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:57.280
The update brought brake confirm and speed profiles to Australian vehicles on firmware 2026.16.6.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:04.700
HW4 cars received the software first, while HW3 vehicles remained ineligible for now.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.000
Owners in right-hand drive markets have begun testing the features on local roads.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:16.420
The rollout covers only a small percentage of the global fleet so far. Reports also suggest

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:23.240
Tesla may bring the stretch 3-row Model YL to North America before July 4th.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.000
The vehicle would add a third row while staying on the current Model Y platform.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.740
Pricing and range figures have not been confirmed and Tesla has not issued an official statement.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:38.760
The timing would address buyer segments left open after the Model X left production.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:44.100
Tesla added an expandable trunk organizer to its official shop for the Model Y

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:50.760
at a price of $245. The product creates divided compartments for cargo management.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:55.240
It joins other official accessories aimed at improving daily usability.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.800
Owners can order the item directly through the Tesla app or website.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.540
The launch continues Tesla's pattern of selling vehicle specific add-ons through its own channels.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.900
Tesla launched a competition that rewards winners with lifetime free supercharging.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:15.620
Participants must complete specific in-app challenges or driving goals.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.420
The program gamifies charging behavior across the fleet.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.940
Winners receive the benefit tied to the individual vehicle.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.280
The initiative seeks to increase engagement with Tesla's charging network.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:32.560
Unplugged performance released their retro futuristic wheel design for the Cybertruck.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:40.140
The 24-inch C-well-abrid disc. Wheels feature a disc style spoke pattern that updates the vehicle's appearance.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:44.200
Owners can order the set directly from the aftermarket supplier.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:49.040
The launch adds to a growing list of third-party styling options for the pickup.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:54.320
The wheels maintain compatibility with the Cybertruck suspension and braking hardware.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:08:00.120
An owner reported completing a full year of scheduled service on their Tesla in one session.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:04.680
The post highlights how owners track maintenance intervals through the vehicle app.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:11.280
Tesla's service model relies on over-the-air updates and fewer moving parts than ICE vehicles.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:16.600
This approach reduces the frequency of dealer visits compared with traditional cars.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:23.220
Owners continue to share these experiences on X as a way to document real-world ownership costs.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:29.860
Multiple recent crash reports did not name the vehicle make or model in headlines or early paragraphs.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:35.720
The observation points to inconsistent media practices when covering incidents involving

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:41.600
different brands. Tesla vehicles often receive explicit branding in similar coverage.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:45.500
The pattern affects how readers initially perceive the story.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:51.360
Community discussion on X centers on whether this omission changes the tone of reporting.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:56.140
Now, one thing worth watching is the dealership fire in Maryland.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:02.520
Four vehicles burned at the Owings Mills store and the incident raises questions about how inventory

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:09.540
is stored and charged at retail locations. Tesla has not released details on the cause or any

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:15.980
adjustments to site protocols. Such events remain rare yet they draw extra scrutiny to operational

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:22.320
practices even when the overall safety records stay strong. The company has systems in place to

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.620
investigate and adapt, which has helped manage similar low-frequency issues in the past.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:34.800
Dry electrode manufacturing promises smaller factory footprints and no solvent handling, yet the

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:41.100
binder has remained a hidden vulnerability. Lithium ions and electrons can strip fluorine from

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:48.400
PTFE, leaving brittle carbon that weakens the electrode web over time. Tesla's patent wraps each

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:54.040
binder particle in a protective coating before the film is formed, using mechanical fusion rather

00:09:54.040 --> 00:10:00.160
than wet chemistry. The coating keeps the solvent free process intact while adding an ion blocking

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:07.520
yet electron conducting layer that can reach 90% surface coverage. Materials such as carbon black or

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:13.880
copper provide conductivity so electrons still move through the electrode while lithium ions stay

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:20.180
away from the polymer core. Because the coating is applied dry, the sequence stays compatible with

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:27.520
high-speed roll-to-roll lines already installed at Giga Texas and Nevada. For cost per catter-hour

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:33.700
targets, any chemical failure mode that shortens pack life would erode the margin advantage dry

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:40.240
electrodes are meant to deliver. Before we go, keep an eye on whether coated binder electrodes appear

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:45.560
in production packs and how their cycle life numbers compare with current cells. That's your

